  "question": {
    "text": "In a solid 'AB' having rock salt arrangement ( <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> structure), 'A' atoms occupy the corners and face center of the cubic unit cell. 'B' atoms occupies all octahedral voids of the unit cell. If all the face-centered atoms along one of the axes are removed, then the resultant stoichiometry of the solid is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "kj3pT",
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "o7v2i",
      "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XTjTI",
      "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GiyRe",
      "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "There were 6 A atoms on the face-centres removing face-centred atoms along one of the axes means removal of 2 A atoms.<br /><br />Now, number of A atoms per unit cell<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/14_que_chem.JPG\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 72px;\" /><br /><br />Number of B atoms per unit cell<br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder></math><br /><br />Hence the resultant stoichiometry is <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
    "image": null
  },
